e absent from MIM''s label index, so CultureMech could not resolve them: ''Fe(III)・EDTA'' (x3 CultureMech mentions); ''Fe(III)-EDTA (0.66% [wt/vol] in water)'' (x1 CultureMech mentions); ''Fe·EDTA'' (x1 CultureMech mentions). Source: culturemech:output/ingredient_occurrences.tsv.'\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Fe_Iii-edta.after.yaml:151:  changes: 'Isolated source-review proposal ferric-edta: added aliases [''EDTA・Fe(III)'']; rejected provenance labels [] Subject to independent skeptical review and guarded coordinator integration; inherited full-payload support must not transfer.'\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Na3-edta.after.yaml:2:preferred_term: Na3-EDTA\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Na3-edta.after.yaml:5:  ontology_label: EDTA trisodium salt\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Na3-edta.after.yaml:13:    source: all_unmatched_20261107 worker04 primary proposal trisodium-edta\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Na3-edta.after.yaml:14:    notes: The three frozen occurrences explicitly specify three sodium ions. Live CHEBI:63125 defines the trisodium salt, distinct from disodium CHEBI:64734/64758. The owner is correctly trisodium but its active 'EDTA di sodium salt' synonym is chemically wrong. Add the explicit 3Na spelling and retain the wrong disodium string only as rejected provenance; no interpretation of case125 is imported here. Original NBRC387/900/391 all corroborate3Na-EDTA; NBRC387 specifies200mg in a vitamin stock, not the frozen200g/L flattened component. Evidence and exact frozen scope are recorded in reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/fragments/chemistry-decisions.json. This proposed delta does not approve complete owner/export payload or remove inherited holds.\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/proposals/chemistry/Na3-edta.after.yaml:16:- synonym_text: EDTA-3Na\nreports/all_unmatched_20261107/